  Supersedes the 2026-06-30 capture (SHA cbb395f, xppc 7.0.7858.27).

  Why it was re-captured, and it is not a cosmetic difference:
  The case instruction asks for a field group 'Overview' containing NoteId and
  Subject, and says exactly why - "a form whose grid names a field group the
  table does not declare fails FormPatternValidation at build time". The old
  golden carried <FieldGroups /> and satisfied neither. The cause was a create-path
  defect: <FieldGroups> was a hardcoded literal, so properties.fieldGroups was
  dropped without a word. Three cases in golden-build-verification.json failed on
  exactly that (L1-form-basic, L1-form-detailsmaster, L1-form-simplelistdetails -
  all three bind a grid to this table's Overview group).

  The index arrives the same way now: <Indexes> was a literal too, and the repair
  the tool offered (add-index) needs the C# bridge, so on the template path an
  index could not be produced at all.

  Shape changes from the older capture, both from the writer, neither a
  regression: the <Declaration> is present (the 2026-06 capture came from the
  bridge, which omits it), and the five standard Auto* field groups are written.

  Build: 0 errors, xppbp clean. Sandbox rolled back.
  PENDING HUMAN REVIEW (see docs/AGENT_EVAL_LOOP.md 6.4).
-->
